int $(3,4)$ is at a distance of $4$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(3,1)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $4-1=3.$"} :step/id #uuid "12252c44-f6ed-5a4c-877a-529ad585fdea" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527255}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527243 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068e3080-4337-581d-9b8b-cc0e663f7828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526516} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1c255d-9fb4-5411-b2aa-255dce8090e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526524} {:answer/id #uuid "155fbdce-2870-53b4-bdf7-758d24346ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526545} {:answer/id #uuid "21bbce83-c3c6-5f3b-ac9d-a19684c5d630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526575} {:answer/id #uuid "b70f45a0-ba84-55de-ab9d-38674206db65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526516} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba2c0b6c-0868-582f-9fb0-8f7239a4a7d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3ab19b4a-4627-54ee-8e9e-8d051f6ac141" :question/math-academy-id "q-61265" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-3,2)$  and $(-3,-4)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/c0/c0dcef8b6c0c63e17fc9b516e3e3176f054dd0eddb93c71375a3de3272da9623.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](images/c1/c1764499f4600d5c74c598b205e0a1971ca91231c4464f77e0809a680003bf11.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/5b/5b4c4c665b07575604dc873703517548404d7c31e8395070642ca37584c6d08f.png)\n\nThe point $(-3,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-3,-4)$ is at a distance of $4$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $4+2=6.$"} :step/id #uuid "35f258ab-51ea-5cc4-ab06-dadec569e07a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527255 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "199f5bd1-cf24-5ec5-87fb-e715dfad0524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526557} {:answer/id #uuid "4446140c-ebf8-5421-a61b-bfae02059671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526633} {:answer/id #uuid "7e700299-d0cc-5e63-95d1-97a04cb6ea9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526752} {:answer/id #uuid "921e2d09-f58f-50dc-91f3-e6324b399fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526789} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd79885-eb4b-5b18-8642-27db39ab655a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526557} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a86d0ab-34e6-5c19-97fc-00a0a1fc39ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "67699b33-3e46-5c7c-ad2b-2f6df6bd8eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-61105" :question/problem "![](images/25/25e1891ce31fa7043723b2dcb4cd1e01c41dbd82ae70ef5024c64ed2d6deab33.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(-3,1)$  and $(-3,-5)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](images/1f/1f3eeede9aa301cf6d64b48cc86f770fc86517ed51285da9bdc86e5a580b243f.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/a5/a504ca22769a377cd7e23e0b6a09595d00c8ad25733f3d1e6a716b52f262e139.png)\n\nThe point $(-3,-5)$ is at a distance of $5$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-3,1)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $5+1=6.$"} :step/id #uuid "5c465ab7-ebb0-5979-8fd6-300e20ddd25b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527287}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527287 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff3933f1-5330-5a93-bd06-b1a968921e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073029} {:answer/id #uuid "038610b4-8855-5613-ad62-a56e0c0f24e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073030} {:answer/id #uuid "288f063e-1947-5a0f-8867-d300a95793d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073031} {:answer/id #uuid "3d64ff07-ead1-5334-9540-a844d96b19ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073032} {:answer/id #uuid "4eced26e-1801-553d-a9a9-d047aee0b82a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073033}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073031} :answer-field/id #uuid "723fead1-3866-508a-9080-2df0ed86113b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3943d606-fff6-5e9c-a446-2d4378743487" :question/math-academy-id "q-61224" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(4,2)$  and $(4,8)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/66/66c988b7fede0e97eae46388dd0e57aee2c49a3c185c9a888277da8fefc947ab.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](images/63/63f70c20c918dae51ecddc7891a8cbee7c5749720521e62fe26e9bc4e33bb9e6.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/d3/d3693b8c3d07636143b2c77c3bd2645015885b77ec4e8ddffde2e121da0511bc.png)\n\nThe point $(4,8)$ is at a distance of $8$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(4,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $8-2=6.$"} :step/id #uuid "f27b2fa2-b4cf-5259-af6d-f395c41888da" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527243}}] :activity/title "Distances Between Points in the Coordinate Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526490}]}
